Shared memory daemon (spec 0113 delta-02): defaulting claude to HTTP.
  Without it, every session spawns its own memory server and only the
  first one to write can write — the rest are refused for their whole life.
  claude now reaches shared memory through the daemon.

  NOTE: this run switched claude only. Still on the previous arrangement:
    - copilot
    - antigravity
  They will contend for the memory lock with claude until they switch too.
  Switch the whole machine at once with: task mempalace:switch-http

  Restart any running claude session to pick this up.

